   "summary": "The Edo State Police Command on Monday confirmed the killing of an All Progressives Congress chieftain, Julius Bello, by his son, Irobudo. The state police spokesperson, Eno Ikoedem, who confirmed the killing in a statement, said the suspect was still at large, adding that an investigation had commenced into the incident. He was reportedly hacked to death by his son, who allegedly used a sledgehammer to hit him on the head.",
   "summary_zh": "埃多州警察司令部周一证实，进步大会党地方领袖朱利叶斯·贝洛被其儿子伊罗布多杀害。州警察发言人埃诺·伊科埃德姆在一份声明中证实了这起遇害案，并称嫌疑人目前仍逍遥法外，调查工作已经启动。据报道，他被儿子用大锤击中头部，当场被砍死。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Edo State Police Command on Monday confirmed the killing of an All Progressives Congress chieftain, Julius Bello, by his son, Irobudo. The state police spokesperson, Eno Ikoedem, who confirmed the killing in a statement, said the suspect was still at large, adding that an investigation had commenced into the incident. “The police have commenced an investigation into the matter, and the suspect is currently at large,” she added. The deceased, popularly known as De Lord Ogata, was the APC Ward Three Chairman in Fugar, Etsako Central Local Government Area. He was reportedly hacked to death by his son, who allegedly used a sledgehammer to hit him on the head. Election tribunal: 375 judges take oath, parties insist on fairness Tinubu fit for 2027 race, APC chairman dismisses health concerns Kebbi gov reinstates suspended commissioner A family source said the suspect returned home from Lagos at the weekend and attacked his father on Sunday. The source said Irobudo was reportedly told by a prophet that his father was responsible for his being poor. “This is a big tragedy. It is so sad that he killed his father over some prophecy. He is currently on the run. The family is mourning right now,” the source added. Adeyinka Adedipe",
