   "summary": "North Korea has test-fired a new type of torpedo in the East Sea, state media reported Tuesday, saying it plans to deploy the system with its Navy in early 2027. The Academy of Defense Sciences, the Missile Administration and the Torpedo Weapon Research Bureau \"verified the combat effectiveness\" of the new high-speed torpedo system Monday, the Korean Central News Agency (KCNA) said. The North gave no further details on the torpedo's specifications.",
   "summary_zh": "朝鲜官媒周二报道，朝鲜已在东海试射一种新型鱼雷，并计划于2027年初将该系统部署到海军。朝鲜中央通讯社（KCNA）称，国防科学院、导弹管理局和鱼雷武器研究局于周一验证了这种新型高速鱼雷系统的“战斗效能”。朝鲜没有进一步披露该鱼雷的具体规格。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "North Korea has test-fired a new type of torpedo in the East Sea, state media reported Tuesday, saying it plans to deploy the system with its Navy in early 2027. The Academy of Defense Sciences, the Missile Administration and the Torpedo Weapon Research Bureau \"verified the combat effectiveness\" of the new high-speed torpedo system Monday, the Korean Central News Agency (KCNA) said. The test was part of the \"obligatory activities\" of the defense research institutes to put weapons technology \"on a highly-developed basis,\" it added. The North gave no further details on the torpedo's specifications. Pyongyang has been pushing to strengthen its naval capabilities with a string of weapons tests. Last month, it conducted an underwater test of a new high-speed, precision-guided torpedo that uses artificial intelligence (AI) technology, calling it a \"significant\" change in its naval capabilities. It also fired two types of strategic cruise missiles from what was presumed to be a 3,000-ton submarine in the East Sea. In June, it commissioned the 5,000-ton Choe Hyon destroyer in the West Sea, followed by the 5,000-ton Kang Kon destroyer in the East Sea in September",
