   "summary_zh": "第13届尼日利亚法律奖将表彰那些为塑造尼日利亚企业、金融和经济格局作出贡献的杰出律师、商业领袖和机构。该奖项由《ESQ法律实践杂志》出版商ESQ Trainings Limited主办，将于2026年11月15日星期日在拉各斯维多利亚岛的Landmark Event Centre举行。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The 13th edition of the Nigerian Legal Awards will recognise outstanding Lawyers, business leaders and institutions whose contributions have shaped Nigeria’s corporate, financial and economic landscape. The awards, organised by ESQ Trainings Limited, publishers of ESQ Legal Practice Magazine, will hold on Sunday, November 15, 2026, at the Landmark Event Centre, Victoria Island, Lagos. Among prominent personalities billed for recognition are Plateau State Governor, Caleb Mutfwang; former Minister of State for Petroleum Resources and Foreign Affairs, Odein Ajumogobia, SAN; Group Chief Executive of Oando Plc, Adewale Tinubu; and Senator Adeniyi Adegbonmire, SAN. Institutions expected to receive recognition include, the Nigerian Communications Commission and the Securities and Exchange Commission. According to the organisers, this year’s edition will place particular emphasis on major financial and commercial transactions undertaken between August 2024 and September 2026, highlighting the legal expertise behind investments, acquisitions, financing arrangements and corporate restructuring. Notable transactions include the $1.35 billion financing facility secured for Dangote Industries Limited, the Heirs Group’s acquisition of a 20.07% stake in Seplat Energy, and the $750 million acquisition involving Geregu Power Plc. Other transactions include the change of ownership at Eko Electricity Distribution Company, and UAC of Nigeria Plc’s acquisition of CHI Limited. Founder of ESQ Trainings Limited and Convener of the awards, Lere Fashola, said the initiative seeks to highlight the critical role Lawyers play in business growth and economic development. He explained that technology had strengthened the nomination and evaluation process, while independent judges would retain responsibility for determining award recipients. Founded on January 22, 1995, THISDAY is published by THISDAY NEWSPAPERS LTD., 35 Creek Road Apapa, Lagos, Nigeria with offices in 36 states of Nigeria , the Federal Capital Territory and around the world. It is Nigeria’s most authoritative news media available on all platforms for the political, business, professional and diplomatic elite and broader middle classes while serving as the meeting point of new ideas, culture and technology for the aspirationals and millennials. The newspaper is a public trust dedicated to the pursuit of truth and reason covering a range of issues from breaking news to politics, business, the markets, the arts, sports and community to the crossroads of people and society. You can email us at: hello@thisdaylive.com or visit our contact us page",
