   "summary": "The party’s Zonal Campaign Coordinator for the North-East and North-Central, Babachir Lawal, said the party would not remain passive in the face of violence directed at its supporters. Lawal, in a video seen by LEADERSHIP via X, said the party’s commitment to peaceful political engagement should not be mistaken for an unwillingness to defend its members.",
   "summary_zh": "该党东北和北中部分区的竞选协调员巴巴希尔·拉瓦勒表示，面对针对该党支持者的暴力行为，该党不会坐视不管。拉瓦勒在LEADERSHIP通过X看到的一段视频中表示，该党对和平参与政治的承诺，不应被误解为其无意保护本党成员。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The party’s Zonal Campaign Coordinator for the North-East and North-Central, Babachir Lawal, said the party would not remain passive in the face of violence directed at its supporters. Lawal, in a video seen by LEADERSHIP via X, said the party’s commitment to peaceful political engagement should not be mistaken for an unwillingness to defend its members. He said the NDC would not allow its supporters to be subjected to violence simply because its political leaders, Peter Obi and Rabiu Kwankwaso, were committed to peaceful engagement. “We will not turn the left cheek for you to slap after slapping the right one. We are not going to be docile to absorb any violence targeted at us and our supporters just because Mr Peter Obi and Rabiu Kwankwaso are peace-loving gentlemen,” he said. The former Secretary to the Government of the Federation added that the party would not remain silent over attacks against its members. His remarks come amid growing political realignments and preparations by parties and political groups ahead of the 2027 elections. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
