   "title": "South-East Security Has Improved Under Tinubu, Says Shettima",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/south-east-security-has-improved-under-tinubu-says-shettima/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Mon, 09 Nov 2026 20:23:00 +0000",
   "_dt": 1794255780.0,
   "ageDays": 0.15,
   "summary": "Shettima gave the assurance on Monday during the All Progressives Congress (APC) presidential campaign rally in Abakaliki, Ebonyi State, where he highlighted the administration’s security interventions and infrastructure investments in the South-East. “The security of the South-East has changed since President Bola Ahmed Tinubu became Commander-in-Chief over three years ago.",
   "summary_zh": "谢蒂马周一在埃博尼州阿巴卡利基举行的进步大会党（APC）总统竞选集会上作出保证，并介绍了政府在东南部采取的安全措施和基础设施投资。“自博拉·艾哈迈德·蒂努巴总统于三年前就任武装部队总司令以来，东南部的安全形势已经发生变化。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Shettima gave the assurance on Monday during the All Progressives Congress (APC) presidential campaign rally in Abakaliki, Ebonyi State, where he highlighted the administration’s security interventions and infrastructure investments in the South-East. In a statement by his spokesman, Stanley Nkwocha, he said the Tinubu administration recognised that sustainable economic development could only thrive in an environment where communities, businesses and critical infrastructure were adequately protected. “The security of the South-East has changed since President Bola Ahmed Tinubu became Commander-in-Chief over three years ago. We have worked to restore order, and we will keep working,” the Vice President said. Shettima identified the establishment and commencement of operations at the Nigerian Army Recruits Training Depot at Amasiri–Edda in Ebonyi State as one of the Federal Government’s interventions to strengthen security in the region. He said the administration’s broader development agenda was also aimed at addressing the economic and social challenges that have constrained the South-East’s growth. According to him, the Federal Government is investing in transport infrastructure, agriculture, green energy, housing and human capital development to improve economic opportunities and strengthen regional integration. He also highlighted the establishment of the South-East Development Commission, the launch of the South-East Vision 2050 and the approval of the South East Investment Company as initiatives designed to accelerate regional development and attract investments. Shettima maintained that the Tinubu administration had demonstrated its commitment to Ebonyi State through federal projects, appointments and programmes aimed at improving citizens’ welfare. He urged the people of the state to support Tinubu’s re-election bid in 2027, saying the administration deserved another mandate to consolidate its development programmes. Governor Francis Nwifuru, who also spoke at the rally, commended the President for what he described as special federal interventions in road infrastructure across the state. “Under President Tinubu, the poor roads in our state and zone are now better. We now enjoy special road interventions,” the governor said. Nwifuru, however, appealed to the Federal Government to support the provision of a 330kV electricity transmission line to improve power supply across Ebonyi State. He subsequently pledged that the state would deliver 80 per cent of its votes to Tinubu in the 2027 presidential election. Also speaking, Minister of Works, Senator David Umahi, praised the President for federal investments in road infrastructure across Ebonyi, expressing confidence that the state would deliver 1.3 million votes to Tinubu in the forthcoming election. Former APC National Chairman, Senator Adams Oshiomhole, also commended the administration’s economic reforms and infrastructure investments. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates → Join Our WhatsApp Channel --> --> Jonathan Nda-Isaiah Jonathan Nda‑Isaiah is the Political Director at LEADERSHIP Newspaper and serves on the Editorial Board. Specialising in political reporting and editorial writing, he offers deep insights into governance, policy and national affairs. His analysis is known for its depth and balance, reflecting a strong commitment to accurate, thought‑provoking journalism that influences public discourse in Nigeria",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
