   "title": "CJ Olive Young to open 5 more US stores by mid-2027, expanding to San Diego",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/business/companies/20261109/cj-olive-young-to-open-5-more-us-stores-by-mid-2027-expanding-to-san-diego",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Mon, 09 Nov 2026 05:57:02 GMT",
   "_dt": 1794203822.0,
   "ageDays": 0.75,
   "summary": "CJ Olive Young, Korea’s largest health and beauty store chain, will open five more stores in California by the first half of 2027, bringing its U.S. total to seven, the company said Monday. Olive Young said its stores also introduce shoppers to product types common in Korea, such as sunscreen sticks, cushion compacts that dispense sunscreen through a sponge, and toner pads, which are cotton pads presoaked in skin toner.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国最大的健康美容零售连锁店CJ Olive Young周一表示，将在2027年上半年之前于加利福尼亚州再开设5家门店，使其在美国的门店总数达到7家。Olive Young表示，其门店还向顾客介绍韩国常见的产品，例如防晒棒、通过海绵 dispensing 防晒霜的气垫粉饼，以及预先浸有爽肤水化妆水的化妆棉。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "CJ Olive Young, Korea’s largest health and beauty store chain, will open five more stores in California by the first half of 2027, bringing its U.S. total to seven, the company said Monday. The retailer opened its first U.S. store in Pasadena in May and a second at Westfield Century City in Los Angeles in June. Four of the new stores will be in the greater Los Angeles area: Spectrum Center, a lifestyle shopping center in Irvine; Del Amo Fashion Center in the South Bay area; Bloom on 3rd, a shopping complex near the Farmers Market in central Los Angeles; and Brea Mall in Orange County. The fifth will open at Fashion Valley in San Diego, its first outside the Los Angeles area. Opening dates for each store have not been set. Three of the sites — Del Amo Fashion Center, Brea Mall and Fashion Valley — are operated by Simon Property Group, a major U.S. mall owner. The company said the expansion will help small and independent Korean cosmetics brands, collectively known as K-beauty, reach American consumers without their own distribution networks. Olive Young said its stores also introduce shoppers to product types common in Korea, such as sunscreen sticks, cushion compacts that dispense sunscreen through a sponge, and toner pads, which are cotton pads presoaked in skin toner. Its in-store Skin Scan service, which analyzes a customer’s skin condition and recommends products, had been used by about 27,000 customers as of late October, roughly five months after the first store opened. “Olive Young’s U.S. stores serve as a bridge that helps emerging brands settle into the mainstream market,” an Olive Young official said. This article was published with the assistance of generative AI and edited by The Korea Times",
