   "title": "Nvidia launches investigation into CEO’s affair with suspected Chinese spy",
   "url": "https://www.myjoyonline.com/nvidia-launches-investigation-into-ceos-affair-with-suspected-chinese-spy/",
   "domain": "myjoyonline.com",
   "source": "MyJoyOnline（加纳）",
   "published": "Sun, 08 Nov 2026 22:56:00 +0000",
   "_dt": 1794178560.0,
   "ageDays": 1.04,
   "summary": "US tech giant Nvidia has opened an independent investigation following reports that its CEO, Jensen Huang, had a relationship with a suspected Chinese spy. US intelligence officials believed that Chinese businesswoman Alice Huang, who had a close relationship with Jensen Huang, was a spy for Beijing, according to a New York Times report.",
   "summary_zh": "美国科技巨头英伟达启动独立调查。此前有报道称，该公司首席执行官黄仁勋与一名疑似中国间谍有交往。《纽约时报》报道，美国情报官员认为，与黄仁勋关系密切的中国女商人黄艾丽丝是北京派来的间谍。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "US tech giant Nvidia has opened an independent investigation following reports that its CEO, Jensen Huang, had a relationship with a suspected Chinese spy. The company, one of the world's most valuable, said its board had no reason to believe its secrets or national security were compromised, adding that the CEO was committed to continuing to lead the company. Separately, Jensen Huang admitted to having been \"unfaithful\" to his wife and apologised for hurting her and their children. US intelligence officials believed that Chinese businesswoman Alice Huang, who had a close relationship with Jensen Huang, was a spy for Beijing, according to a New York Times report. Jensen Huang said he took \"full responsibility\" for what he did, adding that he had fallen short of his responsibilities to Nvidia's employees, board and shareholders. Nvidia is one of the world's largest companies and is seen as central to making the hardware for emerging AI technologies. Its CEO said: \"I was unfaithful to my wife. My actions hurt her and our children. There is no excuse for what I did. I am deeply sorry.\" His statement continued: \"Regarding the national security concerns raised in news reports, Nvidia's Board of Directors has initiated an independent investigation. I support the investigation and will cooperate fully. \"I love our country and our company. I am committed to protecting Nvidia and supporting America's national security. I am proud and grateful to be an American.\" A separate statement issued by Nvidia's board of directors said it would begin an investigation in \"light of recent reporting that founder and CEO Jensen Huang has been the target of a foreign intelligence effort\". It continued: \"The Board prioritises US national and economic security, which is paramount to the interests of Nvidia and its shareholders. Alice Huang, who is of no relation to Jensen Huang, is linked to Singapore-based data centre firm Megaspeed. The company told the New York Times last month its current leadership took the allegations seriously and had appointed external legal advisers to conduct an internal investigation. Nvidia is a central player in AI infrastructure, providing chips to leading AI model developers including OpenAI and Meta. The microchip manufacturer is worth some $4.5 trillion, making it one of the most valuable companies ever. China previously rejected allegations of an espionage operation targeting Nvidia's chief, calling the claims \"groundless speculation\" . US intelligence agencies monitored Alice Huang and concluded she was acting on behalf of the Chinese government, according to unnamed sources cited by The New York Times. Surveillance reportedly revealed communications between Alice Huang and an American citizen, who was subsequently identified as Jensen Huang through a process known as \"unmasking\". It remains unclear what information Alice Huang – who is also known as Huang Le – allegedly passed to Beijing, how valuable it was, or when she is believed to have begun gathering intelligence. Alice Huang did not respond to the paper's request for comment. Last week, members of Congress wrote to Jensen Huang, asking him to appear before them in the light of the reported relationship. Three House Republican committee leaders asked the CEO to appear later in the month, to talk about Nvidia's \"security protocols against foreign adversary espionage\" given his reported relation Alice Huang. \"Recent reports raise significant national security concerns regarding the PRC's [China's] access to sensitive US technology and information. \"The issue of PRC infiltration and access to cutting-edge US technology is core to the investigative work of our three committees this Congress,\" the letter said. Nvidia's AI chips have been a major focus of the rivalry between the US and China, and Washington has previously imposed controls on where its advanced products can be sold. The H200, Nvidia's second most advanced semiconductor, had previously been restricted by Washington over concerns that it would give China's technology industry an edge over the US. In January, the Trump administration said it would allow the company to sell its H200 chips to Chinese customers under certain conditions",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
