   "title": "US military officials visit HD Hyundai shipyard to assess shipbuilding capabilities",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/defense/20261108/us-military-officials-visit-hd-hyundai-shipyard-to-assess-shipbuilding-capabilities",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:37:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1794148623.0,
   "ageDays": 1.39,
   "summary": "Senior U.S. Navy and Marine Corps officials have visited Korean shipbuilding giant HD Hyundai Heavy Industries' shipyard to assess its naval shipbuilding capabilities, photos showed Sunday. 4 visit to the shipyard in the southeastern Korean city of Ulsan came as Seoul and Washington are jointly seeking to revive the U.S. shipbuilding industry under the MASGA, or \"Make American Shipbuilding Great Again,\" initiative.",
   "summary_zh": "照片显示，美国海军和海军陆战队高级官员于周日前往韩国造船巨头HD现代重工的造船厂，评估其海军舰艇建造能力。照片拍摄的是官员们参观位于韩国东南部城市蔚山的造船厂；此时，首尔和华盛顿正依据MASGA，即“让美国造船业再次伟大”计划，联手推动美国造船业复兴。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Senior U.S. Navy and Marine Corps officials have visited Korean shipbuilding giant HD Hyundai Heavy Industries' shipyard to assess its naval shipbuilding capabilities, photos showed Sunday. Their Nov. 4 visit to the shipyard in the southeastern Korean city of Ulsan came as Seoul and Washington are jointly seeking to revive the U.S. shipbuilding industry under the MASGA, or \"Make American Shipbuilding Great Again,\" initiative. \"The visit brought together senior U.S. Navy and Marine Corps leaders to assess naval shipbuilding capabilities, installation infrastructure and logistics support across South Korea,\" read a photo caption of one of the uploaded photos on the Pentagon's Defense Visual Information Distribution Service (DVIDS). The delegation included Brendan P. Rogers, assistant secretary of the U.S. Navy for energy, installations and environment; U.S. Marine Corps Lt. Gen. Andrew M. Niebel, deputy commandant for installations and logistics; and U.S. Marine Corps Maj. Gen. Valerie A. Jackson, commander of U.S. Marine Corps Forces Korea. As part of the itinerary, the delegation also assessed opportunities to strengthen maritime sustainment, enhance operational readiness and reinforce the Korea-U.S. alliance, according to DVIDS. In October, HD Hyundai signed an agreement with U.S. engineering and construction company Kiewit to establish a joint venture to build a new shipyard in the United States, with plans to begin construction next year and full-scale operations in 2029",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "kr"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "sec",
    "ene"
   ],
   "tier": 2,
   "actor": "美国",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
   "usHit": true,
   "terrHit": false,
   "riskHit": false,
   "riskKind": "",
